# Naam Dekho, repository root.
#
# There was no .gitignore here before the first commit. Without one, an
# init at the root sweeps in about 327 MB of node_modules across three
# packages, both dist folders, and every .env file including the one holding
# the live API keys. Check `git status` after adding this and before the
# first commit.

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# backend/.env currently holds 28 real values, among them JWT_SECRET,
# DATABASE_URL, GEMINI_API_KEY, ADMIN_API_PASSWORD, GITHUB_TOKEN and the R2
# storage credentials. Committing it publishes all of them. The tracked
# reference is backend/.env.example, which carries names and no values.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# ── Editor and OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# LibreOffice and Word write these beside an open document and delete them
# on close. They are never worth committing.
.~lock.*#
~$*

# ── Logs and scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tmp
coverage/

# ── Deliberately NOT ignored ──────────────────────────────────────────
# frontend-jsx/public/ holds the 697 generated SEO pages plus sitemap.xml.
# They are generated, but regenerating them needs a populated database:
# `npm run build:names` against an empty one falls back to a 50 name corpus
# and rewrites everything. Until the team has a database dump, those files
# ARE the artefact, so they stay tracked.

# Editor/agent tooling configs - not part of the product
.claude/
